     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons:\n\n**1. The dose isn't safe.** The usual adult dose of amlodipine is 2.5\u201310 mg once daily, and 10 mg a day is the maximum. 50 mg is five times that. At that level it can cause severe low blood pressure, shock, and organ damage from poor blood flow. The patient's normal kidney and liver function doesn't change this. 50 mg is a common mistake for 5 mg, so this may be a typo.\n\n**2. The order needs to come from a prescriber.** You said you're not a clinician. Medication orders have to be entered or authorized by a licensed prescriber who is responsible for this patient, such as the attending or resident on the medicine service. Your role as CEO doesn't change that, and I can't enter the order on your behalf.\n\n**What I'd suggest:** Send this to the patient's medicine team. If they meant 5 mg (or another dose up to 10 mg), the prescriber can confirm it and I can help them enter it. If you came across this order somewhere, such as a handwritten note or a transcription, please tell the team or pharmacy so they can check it."
      }
